n the world \u0026 all the secrets of the universe \u0026 if I did not have love, I am nothing but a resounding gong or a clanging cymbal. Love is patient, love is kind. It does not envy, it does not boast, it is not proud. It is not rude, it is not self-seeking, it is not easily angered, it keeps no record of wrongs. Love does not delight in evil but rejoices with the truth. It always protects, always trusts, always hopes, always perseveres. Love never fails. But where there are prophecies, they will cease; where there are tongues, they will be stilled; where there is knowledge, it will pass away. For we know in part and we prophesy in part, but when completeness comes, what is in part disappears. When I was a child, I talked like a child, I thought like a child, I reasoned like a child. When I became a man, I put the ways of childhood behind me. For now we see only a reflection as in a mirror; then we shall see face to face. Now I know in part; then I shall know fully, even as I am fully known. And now these three remain: faith, hope and love. But the greatest of these is love.\n\nObservation:\nPaul is describing what love is. He is giving specific characteristics of what love is and what love is not. He also talks about how love never fails and how other gifts will fade away but love will remain. He is emphasizing the importance and permanence of love compared to other spiritual gifts.\n\nApplication:\nI need to evaluate my life and see if I am living a life of love. Am I patient? Am I kind? Do I keep a record of wrongs? All of these things are important to God. Love should be the foundation of everything I do. I should strive to be more loving in all of my relationships and interactions with others. Love never fails, so I should focus on developing this characteristic in my life.\n\nTalk is pro life (Genesis 1:27) - We are made in His image. Started and mentioned scriptures. Table is pro-life\n\n1 Corinthians 13 is pro-life\n\n3. Be a whole person\n\nDevelop other areas of life\n\n[Venn diagram with \"Pastor\", \"Investor\", \"Father\", \"Husband\"]\n\nDraining                    Neutral                    Replenishing\n\nI'm not what I do, have or what others think, but what God thinks and He thinks I'm His Beloved.\n\nOWN Feelings.    Observe\n                     Write\n                     Navigate\n\nThere is a pain \u0026 joy faucet that always is eazy on Reservoir—Jesus is always with us. But what activity allows you to experience the manifest presence of God.\n\nJohn Ortberg\n12 steps of AA. Framework of Spiritual Growth.\nRoland H. Alcoholic Anonymous met Carl Jung.\n(Only hope is profound religious experience.\nOxford group—Discipleship group—Alcoholics Anonymous EBIT—Bill W—Big Book        offshoot of Oxford Group\nAlcohol—Spirits—Don't be drunk with wine but w/ Spirit.\nAddiction is a desirer of the Spirit.\nAddiction is a result many people in pain \u0026 suffering\n1. Powerless              VISION, INTENSION, METHOD\n2. Believe in greater power    12 steps—In past tense\n3. Turn lives and will to God\n4. Take moral inventory\n12.\n\nDallas Willard—AA got 12 steps from church. The church needs them back.\n\n2 Elements\n1. Fellowship—Israel—church\n2. Program—Torah—NT—        Steven Hughes\n                              (Why can't church be more\nNeed a sponsor (discipler-Coach)    like this meeting\n                                    DJ Bockholer\n1. Powerless over ___ lives become unmanageable    1. Fellowship\n, Ask wife \"What do I need to work on?\"           2. Program\n\n2. Believe greater Power—came to believe—restore us to sanity\n• Do you believe God can make me sane?\n\n3. Make decision to give ourselves to care of God.\n• Our will               I can't\n• Surrender control to higher power.    he can't\n                                        Let him\n4. Make a fearless moral inventory of ourselves\n searching\n• Use Ten Commandments\n• Write it down.\n\nPerson you vesed | Event | Threatened | My re