          "ocr_text": "May 4\nS - For the promise is to you and to your children and to all who are afar off as many as the Lord will call. Acts 2:39\n\nO - God poured out the Holy spirit as a catalyst for revival. I wasn't just for the 120 but for the 2000 and 15 nationals languages. And for their families and many others.\n\nA - We need an outpouring of the Spirit to help us to speak the language of the people around us.\n\nP - God help me to wait long enough every morning to receive the oil to empower me to be a witness.\n\nMay 5th\nS - For if we have been united with Him in a death like his we shall certainly be united with Him in a resurrection like his. Rom 8:5\n\nO - Many saints died a death like his and will resurrect like Him. We believe a different gospel that since Jesus suffered, we wouldn't have to. \u0026 Christians who live in fear of covid\n\nA - I should make my purpose to die welle My life is not my own. He died for me. I'll live for Him.\n\nP - God help me to live a spirit filled, spirit empowered life.\n\nMay 6th\nGod created trees, Jesus gave them a purpose. Faith w/o works is dead. Work puts faith into action. Words can be cheap. Till you work.\nEndurance\nRom 5:1-5 Suffering-Pressure-character-patience-hope\n\nHoly Spirit is the Boss in the live stream.\n\n6/3:8\n\nGotive Chapel - is there substance\n\nThe second I think I'm too good for something in good for something nothing\n\nThats not my job - Thats not my workplace\n\nMay 7\nS - Then fear came upon every soul and MANY wonders and signs were done through the apostles. Act 2:43\n\nO - A reverentIal awe is a spirit given by the Holy Spirit. It seemed that this was a Fruit of the day \u0026 Pentecost\n\nA - Is there a healthy fear of God in my own life? The more I read \u0026 study scripture, the more awe I will have. Silence. Solitude.\n\nP - God help me to have a healthy fear of you and to live my life to honor you",
