          "ocr_text": "April 30\nS- The Lord said to my Lord, sit at my right hand till I make your enemies your footstool. Acts 2:34,35\nO- It wasn't just good news of available salvation from sins but bad news that God was going to destroy them. The gospel is grace and truth. Truth that enemies of God will be destroyed and grace that we can be forgiven and become friends of God.\nA- When I share the gospel I must share both sides of grace and truth.\nP- God help me to apply this to my own life and walk in a healthy fear of you.\n\nWho how did Peter get this message? Read to Emmaus?\nHoly Spirit transformed Peter. He transforms us.\n\nWe all speak different languages to our culture. Have I neglected the Holy Spirit in my life.\n\nMay 1\nS- And when this sound occurred the multitude came together and were confused because everyone heard them speak in their own language. Acts 2:6\nO- They were confused because language was understood by everyone. I spirit - many languages. I spirit many body parts.\nA- We try to find unity through structure and sameness. But God unites in heart even though there are many diverse gifts and parts.\nP- God help me to see that unity of spirit is the most important for unity.\n\nMay 2\nS- So continuing daily with one accord in the temple and breaking bread from house to house they ate their food with gladness and simplicity of heart. Acts 2:46\nO- There was a unity the church had in loving people more than things. They shared what they had and lived very simple lives.\nA- We tend to complicate things. They went door, house to house. They shared resources, gave to one another had to the poor. How much resources are in the church right now?\nP- God help us to have oneness of heart and a clear vision of how to help our island\n\nMay 3\nS- Praising God and having favor with all the people. And the Lord added to the church daily those who were being saved. Acts 2:47\nO- The love and simplicity of these people were attractive to the world and the church grew as God added to them.\nA- Generosity was a key element of the early church. People could have wanted to be a part just to be provided for. But the Lord added. Net men.\nP- God help our community to grow in selflessness and simplicity before we try to grow in numbers.",
