          "ocr_text": "April 26\nS- For you will not leave my soul in Hades, Nor will you allow your Holy one to see corruption. Acts 2:27\nHeGreeted in this spoke concerning the resurrection of the Christ, that the soul was not left in Hades, nor did his flesh see corruption. This Jesus was God has raised up of which we are all witnesses. Acts 2:32\nO- Jesus' body was raised and is on the right hand of the Father. Soul went to Hell. Body resurrected, sitting at right hand of the Fathers.\nA- My hope is the resurrection. A new incorruptibility. Soul in heaven. Incorruption on earth. Body raised when Christ returns.\nP- God help me to communicate this clearly.\n\nApril 27\nS- Therefore let all the house of Israel know assuredly that God has made this Jesus, whom you crucified both Lord and Christ Acts 2:36\nO- They were pricked to their hearts. They were so convicted by what they had done that they wanted to know what they need to receive salvation and be Forgiven but also to be disassociated from the \"House of Israel\" that crucified Jesus.\nA- Peter said, Repent, Be baptized, receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.\nP- God please help us to have the faith of the early church. To believe in the resurrection and to live in a way that will change our culture.\n\nApril 24\nS- Now all who believed were together and had all things in common. Acts 2:44\nO- There was great generosity because of the salvation of Jesus\nA- Generosity will be the result of real conversion from a real presentation of the gospel.\nP- God help\n\nApril 29\nS- And with many other words he testified and exhorted them saying \"Be saved from this perverse\" generation Acts 2:40\nO- We aren't just saved from our sin or saved from the penalty of sin but saved from a perverse generation.\nHe showed that this generation was so far bent the way it was crucified by Israel, and Israel would be judged. He linked their sin against God and showed how bad that sin was and the judgement coming because that sin.\nA- Most don't see how this generation is sinning against God. Evolution credits chance instead of acknowledging a creator. DEI erases sin. No God. No sin. No accountability. What sins are we committing against God? What will He judge us for?\nP- God help me to share your Word in a way that cuts to the heart. Help me to see my need for you in every area of my life.",
