          "ocr_text": "May 16\nS- When they heard these things they were cut to the heart and they gnashed at him with the teeth. Acts 7:54\nO- Interesting that they were \"cut to the heart\" just like the 3000 in Acts 2, but instead of repenting, they killed. Same message. Same conviction. Same spirit. Different response.\nA- I'm not responsible for the response. Just give a clear presentation. Each one is responsible for how they respond to the gospel.\nP- God, what help me to present the gospel clearly to the people you have called me to.\n\nMay 17\nS- Then Peter said to her, \"How is it that you have agreed together to test the Spirit of the Lord? Look the feet of those who have buried your husband are at the door and they will carry you out\" - So great fear came upon all the church and upon all who heard these things Acts 5:9,11\nO- What was the sin? Lying. When they lied to men, they lied to God. What I do to other believers I do to God. They lied about how much they gave. Seems a harsh punishment. Death is deserving for lying about giving? Doesn't God's grace cover sin? Why death instead of public confession? Why were Sapphiras not killed?\nA- Judgment begins at the house of God. Did they go to heaven? Why would Satan want to fill their hearts to lie? About giving?\nP- God help me not to die. Help me to fear you.\n\nMay 18\nS- So they departed from the presence of the council rejoicing that they were worthy to suffer shame for the name. And every house they did not cease teaching and preaching Jesus as the Christ. Acts 5:41,42\nO- They were counted worthy to suffer. Not having honor or riches. Neither the elders... They were counted worthy to suffer. Not having...\nA- Suffering for Christ is such an honor. And we are chosen for it.\nP- God help me to embrace God's offering and look forward to it.\n\nMay 19\nS- But we will give ourselves to prayer and to the ministry of the Word - Then the word of God spread and the number of disciples multiplied greatly in Jerusalem and a great many of the priests were obedient to the faith. Acts 6:4,7\nO- The apostles' main priority was prayer and the Word. Not social responsibility. That was given to responsible Spirit-filled men of good reputation.\nA- Even apostles couldn't do everything. They needed to prioritize prayer and the Word. I seem to have gotten it backwards.\nP- God help me to prioritize prayer \u0026 the word over every other thing in my life.",
