          "id": "ece0fa98-4660-4653-ad6a-56e1bc624939",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-01-13",
          "ocr_text": "Jan 13\nS- If it pleases the king let letters be given to me for the gates of the region beyond the river that they permit me to pass through till I come to Judah and a letter to Asph the keeper of the kings forest that he must give me timber to make beams for the gates of the citadel which pertains to the temple for the city wall and for the house that I will occupy. And the king granted them there to me according to the good hand of my God upon me. Neh 2:7,8\n\nO- Nehemiah knew what he needed to build, knew the supplies he needed and knew the people that controlled the supplies. He had a plan, a list and contacts and prayed for favor and God gave it to him.\n\n4- Chap 1 was speaking his relationship with God. Chap 2 was requesting favor of the king and having a plan that included sequence of building, resources needed and people to give resources. I need to do the same.\n\nP- God please let me accomplish according to your will. Bless me to be a blessing.\n\nJan 14\nS- Then I arose in the night, I and a few men with me. I told no one what God put on my heart to do at Jerusalem. Nor was there any animal with me except the one and which I rode. Neh 2:\n\nO- Nehemiah had supplies from the king and favor of God to rebuild. But he didn't make a big deal about it and told no one going.\n\nA- There is a right time for Public disclosure. It was after gathering resources for the project.\n\nP- God help me to have wisdom 2 call forward in this project.\n\nSan 15\nS- Then I said to them, you see the distress that we are in, how Jerusalem lies in waste, and its gates are burned with fire. Come and let us build the wall of Jerusalem that we may no longer be a reproach. And then I told them of the hand of my God which had been good upon me and also of the kings words that he had spoken to me. So they said, \"Let us wise up and build.\" Neh 2:17,16\n\nO- He starts with their pain. Then the cause of their pain. Then the action to remove the pain. He anticipates their rebuttal but talked it up the king already and shared that after.\n\nA- Start with the problem. Share the solution. Clear objections to the solution.\n\nP- God give me wisdom to serve the next generation of Mavis",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212306638.jpeg",
