        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:54:27.545499+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "45f50b9a-907e-4119-9a7c-7eafd1704bf4",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-05-20",
          "ocr_text": "May 20\nS- And they were not able to resist the wisdom and the Spirit by which he spoke. And they stirred up the people, the elders and scribes and they came upon him and seized him and brought him to the council. Acts 6:8\nO- When unreasonable people fail to reason they resort to violence. History shows that the power of the right idea is greater than death because the pen is mightier than a sword. Truth cannot die unless the bearer of truth is kept silent.\nA- I must have the courage to speak even when its unpopular or am threatened with bodily harm. Threats \u0026 death and death itself tend to be a catalyst to truth when the messenger becomes a martyr.\nP- Lord help me to understand that speak truth in a compelling and courageous way.\n\nMay 21\nS- Therefore those who were scattered went everywhere preaching the word. Phillip went down to the city of Samaria and preached Christ to them... And there was great joy in the city. Acts 8:4,8\nO- People who were scattered didn't lose faith or backslide like some college students but preached everywhere they went and miracles followed.\nA- Are we preaching the same gospel if the people who leave our church leave the faith?\nP- God help us to have the same kind of faith as the early church.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212859017.jpeg",
