        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:46:10.741451+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "40570011-247e-4733-9b23-dad110d380a3",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-01-08",
          "ocr_text": "10. Continue to take inventory. Promptly admit it.\n• Maintain accountability \u0026 self awareness.\n\n11. Sought through prayer and meditation to improve / deepen conscious contact with God. Ask for his will \u0026 power. (Prayer)\n\n12. Having had a spiritual awakening we try to share this with others. We need to share with other alcoholics. We are helped when we help others.\n\nMy weakness helps others more than giftings.\n\nJan 8 - Judgement\n\nS - And they shall go forth and look upon the corpses of the men that transgressed against me. For that worm does not die and the fire is not quenched. They shall be an abhorrence to all flesh. Isaiah 66:24\n\nO - Isaiah closes with the new heaven and new earth, and also the judgement with corpses that do not die in fire and worms.\n\nA - I don't want to end up in hell or whatever place has the corpses.\n\nP - God, I'm scared. I don't want this to be me or anyone I love. Help me to live right and for others to live right.\n\nJan 9\n\nS - For the Lord will not cast off forever, though He causes grief. Yet he will show compassion according to the multitude of his mercies. Lam 3:31,32\n\nO - God will allow us times of mowing, but will also allow us seasons of joy. He is faithful.\n\nH - When things are bad I will praise Him, knowing He is always God and works in all situations.\n\nP - God, thank you for every season and situation in my life. Please fulfill the desires of my heart and fulfill the purpose you have created for me. Amen\n\nJan 10\n\nS - May He grant you according to your hearts desire, and fulfill all your purpose. Ps 20:4\n\nO - If we delight in the Lord He will give us the desires of our hearts. Then He will grant us according to those desires and fulfill the purpose He has for our lives through them.\n\nA - God has called me to embrace the passions He has placed in my heart and pursue them all. As I stop fighting myself God will give me passion and energy to do everything He has called and purposed for me to do.\n\nP - God thank you for giving me a passion for discipleship and for finance and generosity. Help me PLEASE not to blow up. Amen",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212347036.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212347036.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Isaiah 66:24; Lamentations 3:31,32; Psalm 20:4",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:45:58.078+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:54:54.702469+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "f451e684-03d0-4850-a71c-c822a9784710",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-06-05",
          "ocr_text": "June 5\nS- But God demonstrates His love for us in that while we were yet sinners Christ died for us. Rom 5\nO- If we were sinners and Christ died for us, how much more does He love us when we repent and want to follow Him with our lives?\nA- I need to have a confidence in the unconditional love of God that loved me before I did anything for Him.\nP- God please help me to rest completely in your love for me and your finished work on the cross.\n\nJune 6\nS- Knowing that our old man was crucified with Him, that the body of sin might be done away with that we should no longer be slaves of sin. Rom 6:6\nO- When Jesus died, He took upon Himself my sin and now that my sin was crucified, I don't need to be a slave to sin.\nA- Everything I need was provided on the cross. If I am not walking in righteousness and freedom it is because I am not meditating in His word enough.\nP- God please help me to love you and meditate in your word.\n\nJune 7\nS- Like raise you also reckon yourself to be dead to sin, but alive to God in Christ Jesus our Lord. Therefore do not let sin reign in your mortal body that you should obey it in its lust. Rom 6: 11,12\nO- We can decide what we allow to reign in our bodies.\nA- I need to do everything to let righteousness reign in my body. To love God and others through the Power of Christ's love for me.\n\nJune 8\nS- Do the Spirit of God who raised Jesus from the dead dwells in you He also raised Jesus from the dead will also give life to your mortal bodies through His spirit who dwells in you. Rom 8:11\nO- The Spirit that raised Jesus from the dead lives in me and He will quicken my mortal body through the spirit that dwells in me.\nA- If Spirit is in me and is powerful then I should be filled with power and light. Nothing should discourage me.\nP- God please open my eyes to your power in me.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212884570.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212884570.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Romans 5, Romans 6:6, Romans 6:11-12, Romans 8:11",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:54:54.676+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:55:06.994084+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "24180871-70d3-4e89-b132-ac5a11d1c7b5",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-06-01",
          "ocr_text": "June 1\nS- Who then is a faithful and wise servant whom his master made ruler over his household to give them food in due season. Matt 24:45\nO- There is something Jesus is looking for. Wise virgins with oil. Faithful stewards who multiply resource and generous who help the poor.\nA- I need to be pure, vested, waiting with oil in my lamp. Light given from the Holy spirit. I need to multiply talents and give to the needy.\nP- Lord help me to stay close to you to be faithful and generous. Amen.\n\nJune 2\nS- His lord said to him \"Well done good and faithful servant. You were faithful over a few things I will make you ruler over many things. Enter into the joy of the Lord. Matt 25:21\nO- We don't control how much we are given. We just control what we do with what we are given. Then Jesus is the judge of if we were good stewards.\nA- I can't compare myself to others. I must look at myself and Jesus and ask Jesus how I can be better at stewardship\nP- Lord help me to be faithful and wise in everything I do and generous to others. Amen.\n\nJune 3\nS- When the day of Pentecost had fully come they were all with one accord in one place. And suddenly there came a sound from heaven as of a rushing mighty wind and it filled the whole house where they were sitting. Then there appeared to them divided tongues as of fire and one sat upon each of them. And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak with other tongues as the spirit gave them utterance.\nO- Every one was filled with the Spirit. Each one and each one spoke in tongues. It allowed them to speak to one another and understand one another.\nA- The Spirit will help us understand things of God and work in unity with each other.\nP- Where unity is God commands a blessing. Even for evermore.\n\nJune 4\nS- Blessed are those whose lawless deeds are forgiven and whose sin is covered. Blessed is the man to whom the Lord shall not impute sin. Rom 4:7,8\nO- God can forgive and cover sin and that man is blessed who the Lord does not impute sin.\nA- I should be thankful to God everyday for forgiving me and setting me free from sin.\nP- God give me a thankfulness everyday for the blessing of love and forgiveness for everything in my life.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212896273.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212896273.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Matthew 24:45, Matthew 25:21, Acts 2:1-4, Romans 4:7-8",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:55:06.963+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:55:21.554643+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "fc978fe0-39dd-4527-b0e5-b62a9c9fa502",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-06-21",
          "ocr_text": "June 21\nS- Elder then is a faithful and wise servant when his master made ruler over his household to give them food in due season? Matthew 24:45\n\nO- Jesus will be looking for wise virgins and faithful stewards who owe generous to the poor.\n\nA- I remember seeing the poor in Bali and getting upset at God and God said it was my responsibility. God has a vision much bigger than mine. Am I wise with oil? Am I faithful with mammen? Am I generous?\n\nP- God help me to be wise and faithful and generous.\n\nJune 22\nS- The master of that servant will come on a day when he is not looking for him and at an hour that he is not aware of and will cut him in two and appoint him his portion with the hypocrites. There shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth. Mt 24:50-51\n\nO- Jesus does a lot of killing, stomping, cutting binding, throwing, casting out. There is a lot of judgement happening when Jesus comes back.\n\nA- I want to make sure I love Jesus or be loved by Him to be the motive of my stewardship and to be wise with my oil?\n\nP- God help me to understand oil.\n\nJune 23\nS- But the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps. Matthew 25:4\n\nO- Everything on the outside is the same but all in the lamp is evident only to the one who has oil. What this verse does for me is not transferable to anyone else. The Holy Spirit is the one that uses the Word to transform we on the inside. Revelation of the value of my private life before God, my relationship with the Holy Spirit, my time in the Word, my attention, my prayer life, my value-system, my identity, my obedience are all invisible to man, but visible to God and to myself.\n\nAs much as I want this Word to impact others, it is impossible to transfer revelation. It's impossible to transfer transformation. Oil 1) is invisible to others 2) impossible to transfer 3) gives light in the dark 4) Required by Jesus on His return.\n\nA- Work while it is day. For darkness is coming when no one can work.\n\nP- God help me to be a wise servant that has oil in my lamp when you return.\n\nJune 24\nS- A steward the other virgins came also saying, Lord! Open to us! But he answered and said, Assuredly I say to you, I do not know you.\n\nO- Jesus doesn't know those who have no oil. Oil connects to Jesus.\n\nA- I need to know the Spirit in order for Jesus to know me. I need to know Jesus.\n\nP- God help me, to dwell with your Spirit to know Jesus and to allow Him to know me.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212908395.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212908395.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Matthew 24:45",
          "source": "imported",
