          "journal_date": "2025-06-29",
          "ocr_text": "June 29\n\nS- Then he also received one talent came and said, \"Lord I knew you to be a hard man, reaping where you have not sown, gathering where you have not sown seed. And I was afraid and went and hid your talent in the ground. Look, there you have what is yours. But the Lord answered to him, \"You wicked and lazy servant, you knew I reaped where I have not sown, and gathered where I have not scattered seed. So you ought to have deposited my money with the bankers and at my coming I would have received my own w/ interest\n\nO- He knew the master's nature of efficiency but did not emulate it. He despised it and became the opposite of his master. The master expected the servant to be like Him. This is the foundation of stewardship.\n\nA- I need to look at God's nature as the measuring stick of righteousness and have this as my aim. 30,60,100x returns - Flat makes this impossible its an unjust burden on the kingdom of God. If I wouldn't do 100 100x I wouldn't do 30x 60x either\n\nP- God help me to recognize your nature of multiplication and exponential growth. Help me to be more of a faithful steward.\n\nJune 30\n\nS- Therefore take the talent from him and give it to him who has ten talents. Matt 25:28\n\nO- God is a risk manager. He takes from the poor performer and rewards the good performer.\n\nA- I need to have a good balance between the spiritual and the generous. Valuing relationships! productivity and generosity.\n\nP- God help me to live the extremes of all these things.\n\nJuly 1\n\nS- And the king will answer and say to them assuredly, I say to you inasmuch as you did it to the least of these My brethren, you did it to Me. Matt 25:40\n\nO- God calls us to sell what we have to use what we have to make more to take profits and give to the poor among us.\n\nA- I will understand markets, but sell to own oil and give profits to the poor.\n\nP- God help me to be wise, faithful and generous in all I do.\n\nJuly 2\n\nS- Then he will answer them saying \"Assuredly I say to you inasmuch as you did not do it to one of the least of these, you did not do it to me. And these will go away into everlasting punishment but the righteous into eternal life. Matt 25:46\n\nO- Jesus identifies with the poor in the same way we identify with our kids or spouse. When we give to the poor, we give to the Lord\n\nA- The Church should have a daily distribution to the poor. (Hungry, thirsty, sick, prisoner, refugees, widows, orphans)\n\nP- God please help me to be a good steward of everything that you have given to me",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212961727.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212961727.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Matthew 25:24-46",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:56:14.302+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:46:38.583778+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "62eaae7b-8a55-4fc6-98d1-5773aaf6400a",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-01-20",
          "ocr_text": "Jan 20\nS- so I and my brethren servants nor the men of the guard who followed me took off our clothes except that everyone took them off for washing. Neh 4:23\nO- He re-established their will to work by equipping them to face their fears of being killed if they were unmotivated and made encuades at first rubbish, but they were not equipped to fight nor had a plan.\nA- Leaders job is to see the real problem, find the resources, make a plan, give direction to solve the problem then lead by example. His my job to see the real problem, gather resources and make a plan then give clear direction then lead by example.\nP- God help Aali's to be a blessing to our community.\n\nJan 21\nS- Moreover from the time that I was appointed to be governor in the land of Judah from the 20th year until the 32nd year of King Artaxerxes, 12 years neither I nor my brothers ate the governors provisions Neh 4:23\nO- He not only led but saw the financial burden of others and encouraged people not to burden one another but to be generous. He led by restraining his power to prosper himself but to be generous to others \u0026 suffer w/ them.\nA- I need to learn to suffer with others\nP- Help me give what I have.\n\nJan 22\nS- After serious thought, I rebuked the nobles and said to them, \"Each of you are exacting loans from his brother\", so I called a great assembly against them.\nO- Nehemiah thought about the decisions he made, I must give serious thought to all the decisions I make as a leader.\nA- Taught in what how to bring correction. Thought in what is the true problem? Solution? action of leader.\nP- God help me to have your thoughts.\n\nJan 23\nS- Remember me O God, for good according to all that I have done for this people. Neh 5:19\nO- Nehemiah wasn't looking for compassion that was short term or visible, the compassion he rebuild the wall and sacrificed to make it happen and wanted to be rewarded by God.\nA- God remembers every sacrifice we make and He is our rewarder.\nP- God, please help my reward system to align with yours.\n\nJan 24\nS- I am doing a great work so that I cannot come down to you. Why should the work cease while I leave it and go down to you. Neh 6:3",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212385596.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212385596.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Nehemiah 4:23; Nehemiah 5:19; Nehemiah 6:3",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:46:38.523+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:56:23.742035+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "fea4bc90-7d17-4001-80de-eec1efcd6e95",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-06-26",
          "ocr_text": "June 26\nS- Watch therefore for you know neither the day nor the hour in which the son of man is coming. Matt 25:18\n\nO- Jesus says this many times 'Watch'. It's hard to watch for an unexpected event. Like a watchman on the wall. Or looking for a thief.\n\nA- Watching requires looking for signs or any indication His time of return is drawing near. Watching allows me to have an urgency to be prepared. Preparation takes time. Atonement is near.\n\nP- God help me to be ready for when you come back. Help me to watch, pray. Work and keep. Be wise and faithful. \u0026 Generous.\n\nJune 26\nS- For the kingdom of heaven is like a man travelling to a far country who called his own servants and delivered his goods to them. Matthew 25:14\n\nO- God! Faithful stewardship starts by understanding that everything I have is HIS and HE has just delivered it to us for a time.\n\nA- My TIME, TALENT, TREASURE is a result of the generosity, faith, and trust of my master and I will be held to account of how I handle these things.\n\nP- God thank you for my time, talent, treasure that you have given me. Help me not to neglect the gifts you have given to me.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212975634.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212975634.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Matthew 25:18; Matthew 25:14",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:56:23.72+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:46:54.039364+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "a330e8c9-cda7-46ef-a5db-d7f388d9fb53",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-01-16",
          "ocr_text": "Jan 16\nS- But when Sanballat the Horonite, Tobiah the Ammonite official and Geshem the Arab heard of it they laughed at us and despised us and said \"Is this that you are doing? Will you rebel against the King?\" Neh 2:19\n\nO- The enemies of Nehemiah were united by a hatred of Gods people. Nothing else. They saw security of others as insecurity for themselves.\n\nA- I need to know there will be opposition, and prepare for it as well, as rebuttals and prepare for those.\n\nP- God help me to anticipate and prepare for rebuttals, for supply, for enemies.\n\nJan 17\n\nS- Hear O God for we are despised. Turn their reproach on their own heads and give them as plunder to a land of captivity. Neh 4:4\n\nO- Previous chapter Nehemiah breaks the big task into many small assignments and incentivizes each one with a home. Then they prayed through threats.\n\nA- I should break up into small sections and incentivize the work.\n\nP- God give me wisdom to manage this well.\n\nJan 18\n\nS- So we built the wall and the entire wall was built together up to half its height for the people had a mind to work. Neh 4:6\n\nO- The entire project was funded by the king and labor by the people. Work was done by them to build what mattered to them.\n\nA- I need funding. I need cost of materials and labor. I need approval and entitlements.\n\nP- God give me wisdom to lead HALLE VILLAGE\n\nJan 19\n\nS- Never the less we made our prayer to our God and because of them we set a watch against them day and night. Then Judah said \"The strength of the laborers is failing and there is so much rubbish that we are not able to build the wall.\" And our adversaries said \"they will neither know nor see anything till we come into their midst and kill them and cause their work to cease.\" Neh 4:9-11\n\nO- Nehemiah heard what his people were saying but identified why strength was failing. It wasn't the vaguish. It was the threat of death. Once he solved the problem by arming them and a plan of defense they were able to build again.\n\nA- Correctly identifying why someone wont work is key in leadership. What people say is the problem, many times is not.\n\nP- God, help me to have wisdom to discern the real problems.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212399747.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212399747.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Nehemiah 2:19, Nehemiah 4:4, Nehemiah 4:6, Nehemiah 4:9-11",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:46:53.984+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:56:32.293363+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "d722eec6-e2f7-46a1-a537-7b7537d3c55b",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-07-17",
          "ocr_text": "July 17\nS- For this reason I bow my knees to the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, from whom the whole family in heaven and earth is named. Eph 3:14,15\nO- God has a family that is from Adam to Jesus' return. Both on Earth and in heaven. And He will gather us one day and we will meet in the air.\nA- I should live for this day. Make all my decisions based on this day.\nP- God help me to have a vision of this day in my mind.\nRid pay\ndaring second spawn art bag clerk\nskill purse outdoor parade (dry) sean\n\nJuly 18\nS- That He would grant you according to the riches of His glory, to be strengthened with might through His spirit in the inner man Eph 3:16\nO- There is an inner man that can be strengthened by His spirit.\nA- I need an understanding of how to cut off the flesh to strengthen my spirit.\nP- God thank you for walking beside me. Helping me daily to focus on you",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212985152.jpeg",
