        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:56:42.118424+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "5d83bd37-f0ab-4299-bd7d-da7f14178495",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-07-11",
          "ocr_text": "July 11\nS- In Him you also trusted after you heard the word of truth the gospel of your salvation in whom also you believed you were sealed with the Holy Spirit of promise. Eph 1:13\n\nO- I was sealed w the Holy Spirit which is a promise that I will be with Jesus. Sometimes I doubt the power of the Holy Spirit in my life but the scripture says that it is only through the Spirit that I can trust in the gospel and believe in Jesus.\n\nA- I need to spend more time w/ the Holy Spirit and not give him.\n\nP- Holy Spirit, please draw near to us. Help me to love and understand your love for me.\n\nJuly 12\n\nS- The eyes of your understanding being enlightened that you may know the hope of His calling what are the riches of the glory of His inheritance in the saints and what is the exceeding greatness of His power toward us who believe according to the working of His mighty power. Which he w.\n\nO- Pauls desire was that people would be filled with hope to know what their call was. Hope → call → riches/inheritance → power → resurrection\n\nA- The resurrection of Christ shows power that gives us hope of the same resurrection as Jesus if we live like Him.\n\nP- God thank you for the hope that you have given to me about resurrection in my life.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212993471.jpeg",
