        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:57:06.652676+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "4ac65a33-ea47-4dbb-8c30-3ac18348481c",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-07-27",
          "ocr_text": "July 27\nS - That in the ages to come He might show the exceeding riches of His grace in His kindness toward us in Christ Jesus. Eph 2:7\n\nO - He raised us up in heavenly places together made us sit together in Christ Jesus. This scripture shows the spiritual dynamic of a corporate blessing of promotion, rest, rulership, relationship \u0026 revelation of what Christ has done\n\nA - I will do what I can to prioritize relationship with other believers knowing that resurrection, rest, relationship, rulership, \u0026 revelation awaits us. Not just now but forever in Christ.\n\nP - God help me to prioritize relationship with your people over everything.\n\nJuly 28\nS - 1. individual call 2. unity with gentiles, Paul's Christ. 4 - Gifts to Body. S - unity in family. 6 - unity in work -\u003e Spiritual warfare.\n\nO - I wonder why Paul puts family last. And unity w/ gentiles first. I'm missing something.\n\nA - The Jews view of Gentiles was the priority to Paul. He knew that Christ priority was Jew \u0026 Gentile. Seems level of difficulty was the order. I must have peace with God, then race, then church, then family then warfare.\n\nP - God help me to do the difficult things in all my relationships\n\nJuly 29\nS - Nevertheless let each one of you in particular so love his own wife as himself and let the wife see that she respects her husband. Eph 5:33\n\nO - Men want respect and women want love. When men feel disrespected they withhold love.\n\nA - I must always love my wife even if I feel disrespected.\n\nP - God help me to always love my wife no matter how I feel she treats me.\n\nJuly 30\nS - Children obey your parents in the Lord, for THIS IS right. Eph 6:1\n\nO - The word commands us that honor or obedience to parents is Biblical. That we can honor because honor is right.\n\nA - I will have a value based system of honor not merit. I won't wait til a person deserves it to honor them.\n\nP - God help me to always honor those and love you.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213015728.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213015728.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Ephesians 2:7; Ephesians 5:33; Ephesians 6:1",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:57:06.628+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
