        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:58:39.172495+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "cfe6f4d8-5945-45a6-b05a-c5c0f829ef11",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-08-12",
          "ocr_text": "Aug 12\nS- For if we live we live to the Lord and if we die we die to the Lord therefore whether we live or die we are the Lord's. Rom 14:8\nO- Paul made a point that Jesus owns Lord of those who are alive and dead.\nA- I must live for Christ and not to serve myself. It's only through serving Jesus that I can truly live.\nP- God help me die to my flesh and live completely for you.\n\nAug 12\nS- The kingdom of God is not eating and drinking but righteousness peace and joy in the Holy Ghost. Rom 14:17\nO- I want these three things. I don't care about the rules. I want righteousness peace and joy.\nA- I should keep my eyes set on Jesus. He is my righteousness gives peace and joy.\nP- God help me to keep my eyes focused on you.\n\nAug 14\nS- But speaking the truth in love may grow up in all things into him Who is Christ. From whom the whole body joined and knit together by what every joint supplies according to the effective working by which every part does its share causes growth of (the body) for the edifying itself in love. Eph 4:15,16\nO- Every joint has a part to play. To fit, join, grow supply, knit the body together. This happens by speaking truth. Growing in truth.\nA- I need to listen to the truth daily. Speak truth to others so playing my part. I have specific responsibility.\nP- God help me to hear \u0026 understand my part \u0026 do it well.\n\nAug 15\nS- Let no corrupt communication proceed out of your mouth but what is good for necessary edification that it may impart grace to the hearers. Eph 4:29\nO- Paul doesn't stop at not doing bad things but when subtracting bad, add good. The whole chapter talks of replacing evil with good.\nA- Instead of focusing on deleting evil, I need to focus on adding good habits.\nP- God help me to be diligent in what you have called me to be.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213108909.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213108909.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "Rom 14:8; Rom 14:17; Eph 4:15,16; Eph 4:29",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T00:58:39.147+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
