          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-10-16",
          "ocr_text": "Oct 16\nS- And I heard a loud voice from heaven saying \"Behold the tabernacle of God is with men and he will dwell with them and they shall be his people. God Himself will be with them and be their God. Rev 21:3\n\nO- Feast of Tabernacles points to the end of when God will dwell with man again but in a way where we understand and see Him.\n\nA- I understand the wisdom and grace of God. I will rest knowing the God who knew we would rebel and plan that would allow us to be with Him forever.\n\nP- God I thank you that even when I fail, you have a plan to bring me back to yourself?\n\nOct 17\n\nS- But the cowardly, unbelieving, abominable, murderers, sexually immoral, sorcerers, idolaters, and all liars shall have their part in the lake which burns with fire and brimstone which is the second death. Rev 21:8\n\nO- These are the actions that lead to the second death. It's very clear here, who go to hell.\n\nA- I have been all these things in some in more ways. Some in less ways. But I have done all these sins. It's only through Jesus that I can be forgiven and delivered and set free from sin.\n\nP- God help my passion for you to overcome my desire for sin and selfishness.\n\nOct 18\n\nS- But there shall be nothing that defiles or causes an abomination or a lie, but only those who are written in the lambs book of life. Rev 21:27\n\nO- Nothing will be allowed into heaven that is evil or a lie. Only what written in the laws book.\n\nA- There will only be righteousness in heaven. Everything that is evil wont be allowed into heaven.\n\nP- God, I am so unworthy to be called your son. I sometimes wish I could start my life over and do everything correctly. Help me not to be focused on the past, but on the future. Hope\n\nOct 19\n\nS- And behold I am coming quickly and my reward is with me to give to everyone according to his work. Rev 22:12\n\nO- We are not saved BY our works but FOR good works that HE has prepared for us to walk in. We will be judge by how we walked in them.\n\nA- I will not fall into the \"sloppy grace\" mindset but will also not fall into legalism. God saved me for good works that I must be faithful to walk in.\n\nP- God thank you for saving me. Help me to be faithful in all that you have saved me for. Help me not to burn out or to be lazy. Help me to be in love.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213315660.jpeg",
