          "journal_date": "2025-02-06",
          "ocr_text": "Feb 6\n\nS- For bodily exercise profits a little but godliness is profitable for all things having the promise of life that now is and of that which is to come I tim 4:8\n\nO - What exercise profits is awesome but righteousness is greater because it is eternal. Godliness or god-like ness is eternal. God made us in His image. To be like Him is important. Male/Female reflect the image of God. A dual nature- Masculine \u0026 Feminine but one. Father/Son/Holy Spirit. How the Holy Spirit responds to the Father could be the way husband and wife were created to work with one another. Holy Spirit has power, but may has power. Did God give it to man because Eve wanted to be like God?\n\nA- We all need to submit to God. We all need to come under covering. Men need to lead in their homes. Women must submit to husbands. Husbands must love and lead their wives as they submit to Christ.\n\nP- God help me to love \u0026 lead my family. Help my wife to be humble and admit when she is wrong.\n\nFeb 7\n\nS- But if anyone does not provide for his own and especially for those of his own household he is worse than an unbeliever and has denied the faith. 1 Tim 5:8\n\nO- There were actions that showed people have denied the faith. One was not taking care of their own family. Jesus took care of his mother on the cross.\n\nA- If I trust \u0026 have faith in Christ it doesn't\n\n[Right page]\n\nabsolve me of responsibility. I trusted it makes me obligated to the standard of Christ. Jesus, help me to see you in the standard and to want to be like you.\n\nFeb 8:\n\nS- Do not let a widow under sixty's old be taken into the number and let unless she has been the wife of one man. 1 Tim 5:9, 16\n\nO- Paul takes length to identify these who really needed it. He recognized he was called to specifically, help the widows who were contributing and givers. They would be left out if they tried to help everyone.\n\nA- When trying to help everyone, I help no one. I must identify my main target.\n\nP- God help me identify my consumer and my target.\n\nFeb 9\n\nS- Now godliness \u0026 contentment is great gain, for we brought nothing into this world and it is certain we can take nothing out. And having food and clothing with these we shall be content. 1 Timothy 6:6-8\n\nO- Is I pursue godliness and an content that is a great blessing cause being uncontent because I don't have more of something I will completely lose is dumb.\n\nA- I need to be content with what I have but dream for bigger things.\n\nP- God thank you for Jesus' blood and righteousness given to me.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212472176.jpeg",
