          "journal_date": "2025-09-18",
          "ocr_text": "Sept 18\nS- But you have carefully followed my doctrine, manner of life, purpose, faith, long suffering, love, patience and perseverance afflictions, which I endured in Antioch, at Iconium, at Lystra: what persecutions I endured. And out of them the Lord delivered me. Yes and all who desire to live a godly life in Christ Jesus will suffer persecution. 2 Tim2: 10-12\nO- Follow doctrine → manner of life → purpose → faith → patience → love → consistency → affliction and persecution.\nA- Seems that this follows the same pattern of Christ. He is the Word, lived, discipled others then died at the hand of sinners. Direct opposite of retirement.\nP- God help me to love and to be consistent in my faith til death.\n\nSept 19\nS- I knew that he will rise again in the resurrection at the last day. Jesus said to her, I am the resurrection and the life. He who believes in me, though he die he will live. And whosoever lives and believes in me will never die. Do you believe this? John 11: 24-26\nO- There was a belief in a resurrection and a last day in Judaism. Why are we taught so much on eternal life but not about resurrection?\nA- Believing in resurrection to me is so much more exciting that eternity in heaven. God created us for earth. I need to live in the kingdom of God.\nP- God help me to love, serve, obey you as king.\n\nSept 20\nS- For the grace of God that brings salvation has appeared to all men, teaching us that denying ungodliness and worldly lusts we should live soberly, righteously and godly in the present age. Titus 2:11-12. Jesus should live a good life in sobriety and godliness.\nA- I should fill my mind and heart with the Word of God everyday. I need to make a goal of what I'm trying to accomplish or what God wants me to accomplish.\nP- God help me to focus 100% of the time you have given me to love you and love others. To make disciples, to make disciples.\n\nSept 21\nS- Looking for the blessed hope and glorious appearing of our great God and Saviour Jesus Christ, who gave Himself for us that He might redeem us from every lawless deed and purify for Himself His own special people, zealous for good works.\nO- The goal and vision on our minds should be the return of Christ. He died to redeem us from all my junk and purify me to do good acts.\nA- I need to keep my eyes on His return. Looking to live a righteous life to be able to help others live a righteous life.\nP- God help me to be a better disciple who loves, you more and loves others more.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213247099.jpeg",
