          "journal_date": "2025-10-08",
          "ocr_text": "Oct\nSept 8\n\nS - Behold I am coming as a thief. Blessed is he who watches and keeps his garments lest he walk naked and see his shame. Rev 16:15\n\nO - All these bowls of wrath were poured out and the hardness of mans was so great that judgment didn't change their minds or hearts.\n\nA - I hope that every discipline that God gives to me makes my heart softer and more teachable and humble to God. Punishment/Discipline can make people repent or rebel depending on the condition of the heart.\n\nP - God, please continue to give me grace, help me to love you more. I plead or in lack, let me love you more.\n\nOct\nSept 9\n\nS - The ten horns which you saw are ten kings who have received no kingdom as of yet but they receive authority to one have as kings w/ the beast. These are of one mind and they will give their power and authority to the beast. Rev 17:12,13\n\nO - The ten horns could be CEOs not actual kings. having I/mind could be AI. Why would they hate the harlot?\n\nA - These things seem confusing to me right now. I'll put them on the shelf til the Holy Spirit reveals these thing.\n\nP - God please help me to understand your plan for your return.\n\nOct\nSept 10\n\nS - And I heard another voice from heaven saying come out of her my people lest you share in her plagues and lest you receive of her plagues. For her sins have reached to heaven and God remembered her iniquities. Rev 18:4,5\n\nO - Just like God called Israel out of Egypt, Moses out of Egypt, and Lot out of Sodom, God is calling His people out of America. The culture of comfort, selfishness and indulgence. Cities praise refuge for a season, but they become a place of comfort for laziness and sin. Come out. Don't partake in the pleasure of sin. Ble there is a sharing in not just the sin, but the plagues that come with it.\n\nP - God please give me the wisdom and grace to be in the world but not of it. Amen.\n\nOct 11\n\nS - Then a voice came from the throne saying Praise our God all you his servants and those who fear him both small and great. Rev 19:5\n\nO - Status means nothing on the day Jesus returns to judge the living and dead. What matters is that we fear the Lord and live in a way that glorifies Him.\n\nA - I will meditate on His return and live my life in a way that shows I not only love Jesus but also have a reverent fear and awe of Him.\n\nP - Thank you Jesus for loving me and revealing yourself to me. Help me to honor, respect and fear you in all I do.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213261208.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213261208.jpeg"
