        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:02:56.793065+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "1b27cf40-2c42-48c6-8c15-90f96945ab2e",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-10-24",
          "ocr_text": "Oct 24\nS- By this we know love because he laid down the life for us, And we also ought to lay down our lives for the brethren. But whoever has this worlds goods and sees his brother in need and shuts up his heart from him how does the love of God abide in him? I John 3:16-17\nO- The objective of loving one another is through giving value. Time, Talent, Treasure. My focus should be on loving God through giving.\nA- I should make my main focus on how I can live to give \u0026 myself. More of my time talent \u0026 treasure. This starts with an inventory of what I have. Then who God wants me to give to.\nP- God help me to be a good steward of everything that you have given me to steward. You have given me much more than I deserve.\n\nOct 25\nS- In this is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us and sent his son to be the propitiation for our sins. Beloved, if God so loved us, we also ought to love one another. I John 4:10,11\nO- Only the love and life of Jesus can save me from sin. Not just the penalty of sin but from the power of sin itself. Breaking the power of sin takes him, lily to admit I can't do it w/o Christ, but I also cannot do it w/o His body.\nA- I want to live in a way that is love transparent and dependent on Jesus and on others.\nP- God thank you for your grace and love that has the power to transform my heart.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213368981.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213368981.jpeg"
