        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:04:13.833939+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "48baa316-79e4-49b6-9130-64d0100f0710",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-09",
          "ocr_text": "S- Remove your way far from her, and do not go near the door of her house. Prov 5:8\n\nO- The best way to defeat temptation is to get away from it and to live in the light.\n\nA- I need to distance my self from the door of her house. I need to shut the door to strange women.\n\nP- God give me a hatred for sin. A hatred for things that are not of you. Help me to love you more.\n\nNov 9\n\nS- Flee youthful lusts but pursue righteousness. Faith, love, peace with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart. 2 Tim 2:22\n\nO- It's not just about fleeing lust, but pursuing righteousness. Running from bad also running toward.\n\nA- How do I pursue righteousness? Holy Spirit. Faith- The Word. Peace? Sow Peace. Pure heart? Guard my heart.\n\nP- God, help me to guard my heart. Pursue peace. Read my word, and follow the Spirit.\n\nNov 10\n\nS- Here is the word again. FLEE. Sexual immorality. Every sin that a man does is outside the body, but he who commits sexual immorality sins against own body. 1 Corinthians 6:18\n\nO- Here is the word again. FLEE. Sexual immorality. The best way to overcome sexual temptation is to not expose yourself to it. But be near it. To pursue righteousness, faith, love out of a pure heart.\n\nA- I need to put guardians up in my life. Everything should be open and transparent.\n\nP- God help me to live a life of honor, integrity and righteousness.\n\nNov 11\n\nS- Therefore submit to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you. James 4:7\n\nO- We flee temptation. Resist Devil. Submission to God and the Devil will flee from us. We flee temptation. Devil flees from us.\n\nA- I must submit my life to Jesus completely. Submit to Jesus as my Lord.\n\nP- Jesus help me to submit to you. Resist the enemy in my life.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213443720.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213443720.jpeg"
          ],
          "scripture_reference": "2 Timothy 2:22, 1 Corinthians 6:18, James 4:7",
          "source": "imported",
          "summary": null,
          "updated_at": "2026-07-05T01:04:13.762+00:00",
          "visibility": "private"
        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:04:49.793528+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "55423acf-bd26-42b9-ac16-f1c487a33c8a",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-11-20",
          "ocr_text": "NOV 20\n\nS- And not only that but we also stay in tribulations knowing that tribulation produces perseverance, and perseverance character and character, hope. And hope does not disappoint because the love of God has been poured out in our hearts by the Holy spirit who was given to us. Romans 5:3-5\n\nO- Tribulations lead to perseverance, then character then hope. Hope never disappoints b/c of God's love.\n\nA- I can rest assured that all suffering will lead to something good b/c of God's love.\n\nP- God help me to destroy everything in my life that goes against you and your love for me.\n\nNOV 21\n\nS- But God demonstrates his love toward us in that while we were still sinners Christ died for us. Rom 5:26\n\nO- God loves us not because we deserve it, but because he chooses to reveal his unconditional love for us.\n\nA- I should not take advantage of this love but lean into it and be grateful for his love for me.\n\nP- God, so many times I fail to seek you and humble myself because of my love for sin. Help me to fight. Help me to overcome.\n\nNOV 22\n\nS- What shall we say then? shall we continue in sin that grace may abound? Certainly not. How shall we who died to sin, live any longer in it? Rom 6:1,2\n\nO- Just because I'm forgiven of sin doesn't mean it makes sense to keep doing it. I do it because something in me loves it and I need to learn to hate sin.\n\nA- If I'm dead to sin why do I keep returning to it? How do I invite my heart to fear God's name?\n\nP- God please unite my heart to fear you and to love you with 'integrity.\n\nNOV 23\n\nS- For he who has died has been freed from sin. Rom 6:1\n\nO- Dead people don't struggle with sin anymore. If I died with Christ, I should be able to live 24/7 like it's done.\n\nA- God please give me the grace to overcome where Samson, Solomon, and David failed. Help me not to under estimate my enemy.\n\nP- God the tools given to us in this world are extremely powerful and I find myself using them selfishly. Help me to have a dream and vision bigger than the teeth.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213479174.jpeg",
          "photo_urls": [
            "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783213479174.jpeg"
