          "journal_date": "2025-09-04",
          "ocr_text": "Sept 4\nS - And they conquered him by the blood of the lamb and by the word of their testimony for they loved not their lives even unto death. Rev 12:11\nO - The Blood of Jesus is the foundation of our victory. The Word of His testimony, Speaking at what He does for us is the second element and finally the courage to die for our testimony.\nA - I will speak of the testimony I have with Jesus. He gave me a wife, kids, 1st home, 1st rental, 1st house for Million, formation w/Legy, Meeting Bryan, Prophecy \u0026 mercy management, IT mission\nP - God please give me clarity to share w/ boldness the testimony I have with you.\n\nOct 5\nSept 5\nS - IS anyone is to be taken captive, to captivity he goes if anyone is to be slain with the sword with the sword must be slain. Here is a call for the endurance and faith of the saints. Rev 13:10\nO - This is the hour of darkness where authority is given to the enemy. This mirrors the garden of Gethsemane w/ Jesus.\nA - Not my will but thine be done must be my attitude when this time comes.\nP - God thank you that you love me and I pray that I would be able to stand in the day of tribulation to not deny you or my faith in the midst of persecution and trials.\n\nOct 6\nSept 6\nS - Write \"Blessed are the dead who died in the Lord from on. Blessed indeed says the Spirit, that they may rest from their labors and their deeds follow them.\" Rev 14:13\nO - Death is a blessing in the day of tribulation. It is the end of our race. What does it mean that our deeds follow us?\nA - I should look as living for Christ as an invitation to die to myself and my flesh till the day that my spirit is united w/ Christ's before it is reunited with my body in an incorruptible form.\nP - Thank you for the promise of eternal life and the opportunity to lay my life down for you in the same way you laid your life down for me.\n\nOct 7\nSept 7\nS - Then one of the four living creatures gave to the angels 7 bowls full of the wrath of God who lives forever and ever. Rev 15:7\nO - This is a scary picture of God's wrath being given to angels to execute His judgment against His enemies.\nA - I will meditate on the wrath of God as this Day is approaching and getting closer as the return of Christ draws near.\nP - God please instill in me not only an appreciation of your love and grace but also your wrath and judgment.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
