          "ocr_text": "Nov 4\n\nS- He who covers his sins will not prosper. But whoever confesses and forsakes them will have mercy. Prov 28:13\n\nO- There is a fear of confession. That it will be met with condemnation. But God calls me to confess. I can leave the results to Him. Then I must forsake my sin by walking in the light. No secrets.\n\nA- I must confess and forsake my sin. Confess to Jose and the pastors. Forsake by being transparent. This is going to hurt. Hurt many.\n\nP- God give me courage to confess and forsake. To walk in light.\n\nNov5\n\nS- I have made a covenant w/ my eyes why then shall I look upon a young woman. For what is the allotment from God from above and the inheritance of the almighty from on high. Job 31:1\n\nO- Job played out the long game. He recognized a fleshly desire but saw there was nothing there for him in it. And made a covenant.\n\nA- I need to make a covenant w/ myself. Not to allow my eyes to see worthless things.\n\nP- God help me to set my eyes on things above. Not worthless things of this earth.\n\nNov 6\n\nS- Do not be deceived, God is not mocked. For whatever a man sows that he will also reap. For he who sows to the flesh will reap corruption but he who sows to the Spirit will of the Spirit reap everlasting life. Gal 6:7-8\n\nO- Sowing to the flesh will have a result. So will sowing to the Spirit reap everlasting life. The lust of the eyes lust of the body, lust of power. Sowing to the Spirit is prayer. Fasting the Word. Praying in the Spirit. I must\n\nA- I must sow to the Spirit. Spend time in worship, prayer, tongues, in the word. It will have a result.\n\nP- God give me grace to feed my spirit more than my flesh.\n\nNov 7\n\nS- No temptation has overtaken you except such as is common to man, but God is faithful who will not allow you to be tempted beyond what you are able, but with the temptation will also make the way of escape that you may be able to bear it. 1 Cor 6:13\n\nO- Every temptation I face can be overcome. Every time of the enemy has an escape of the Lord.\n\nA- I must look for the door. The escape. The exit. Jesus will sit with me and point to the door if I want it.\n\nP- God, help me to give you my time to sit with you so you can reveal to me my escape.",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
