          "journal_date": "2025-11-29",
          "ocr_text": "S- Therefore, do not let sin reign in your mortal body, that you should obey it in its lusts. Rom 6:12\n\nO- Sin is not Lord. It should not have authority over me and my actions. The battle of sin is in my flesh and mind, but I should live in my life.\n\nA- My God has a will under the Lordship of that need to be put to my flesh and make it subject to the spirit of Christ.\n\nP- God please teach me to put my flesh under the authority of you.\n\nNov 29\nS- And do not present your members as instruments of unrighteousness to sin, but present yourselves as being alive from the dead, and your members as instruments of righteousness to God. for you are not under the law but under grace. Ro 6:13,14\n\nO- I present my body and my will to serve the flesh or the God or sin. I choose to be righteous. It is a choice.\n\nA- I must submit my body under the head of my Lord which that lead to death and righteousness\n\nP- God take will call and emotions for your glory and honor.\n\nNov 24\nS- Shall we continue in sin that grace may abound? Certainly not. Obedience will lead to death. whether we know Christ or not. Rom 6:1,2,E\n\nO- Sin will lead to death. Why do I choose sin over righteousness?\n\nA- the pleasure of fulfilling the flesh can be intoxicating. And addicting. How do I live a obedient life like a controlled life. A life free from\n\nP- Would anyone love what I love? They would if they did what I did. How do I learn to hate sin?",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
