          "ocr_text": "Oct 20\nS- He who testifies to these things says, 'Surely I am coming quickly'. Amen. Even so, come Lord Jesus.\nRev 22:20\n\nO- The Lord Himself promises to come quickly and for us to be aware and alert that the day doesn't take us as a thief.\n\nA- I need to watch and pray and stay alert to what is happening in the world to understand the time we are living in.\n\nP- God please help us to live in a way that is surrendered to you everyday. You alone are worthy of my life.\n\nOct 21\nS- If we say that we have no sin we deceive ourselves and the truth is not in us. If we confess our sins He is faithful and just to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.\n1 John 1:8,9\n\nO- Confession is a part of walking in the light. If I confess my sin, He will forgive and cleanse me of all unrighteousness.\n\nA- I need to have a D group that I am honest and transparent with my sins.\n\nP- God please forgive me of my pride and lack of honesty with you and others about my struggles. Help me to live and think purely.\n\nOct 22\nS- My little children these things I write to you so that you may not sin. And if anyone sins we have an advocate with the Father, Jesus Christ the Righteous. And He Himself is the propitiation for our sins and not for ours only but also for the whole world. 1 John 2:1,2\n\nO- John says to confess sins so that we become free from sin. Not so we can focus on our sin.\n\nA- To be free from sin, I must be honest and transparent about my struggles and sins with others so that I can be free.\n\nP- God I confess my sins to you. Help me to be accountable with trusted brothers.\n\nOct 23\nS- But whoever keeps his word truly the love of God is perfected in him. By this we know that we are in Him. 1 John 2:5\n\nO- The love of God can be perfected in our lives and manifest in us obeying His word. This is evidence we are abiding in Him. If we abide we will bear much fruit.\n\nA- Godlize I must imitate sin, the Love of Christ and allow His love to work in my life til I begin to obey his commands.\n\nP- God thank you for your love that our covers everything in my life.",
