          "ocr_text": "Nov 16\n\nS - When God set forth as a propitiation by His blood through faith, is demonstrate His righteousness, because in his forbearance, God had passed over the sins that were previously committed. Rom 3:25,26\n\nO - I don't understand the mystery of the propitiation of my sin but Jesus is the. He covers my sin with His blood and there His presence rests.\n\nA - I must rest in the grace of God. Not to continue in sin but to enjoy His presence.\n\nP - Jesus, help me to be aware of your presence to live not for righteousness to be righteous but to be with you.\n\nNov 17\n\nS - New to him who works, the wages are not counted as grace but as debt. But to him who does not work but believes on Him Who justifies the ungodly his faith is accounted for righteousness. Rom 4:4,5\n\nO - If I depend on my own righteousness I will always be paying off a debt that will never be paid. But believing on Jesus, my faith is counted as righteousness\n\nA - I must trust Jesus 100% for my righteousness and let my righteousness and freedom flow from that.\n\nP - God help me to focus on what Jesus did for me and to live in righteousness by faith.\n\nNov 18\n\nS - Blessed are those whose lawless deeds are forgiven and whose sins are covered. Rom 4:7\n\nO - Jesus covers my sin. He is the propitiation for my sin and I covered in Him.\n\nA - The more I know Jesus, the more I fall in love with Him and the more I'll hate sin.\n\nP - Jesus, help me to practice your presence and to love you to the point where I hate anything evil everything you call sin.\n\nNov 19\n\nS - It shall be imputed to us who believe in him that did us raised up Jesus our Lord from the dead who was delivered up because of our offenses and was raised up for our justification. Rom 4:24,25\n\nO - Jesus was raised because we have been justified. Through His death our sins have been forgiven and we are justified through His resurrection.\n\nA - I must live in the confidence that all my sins, past present, and future have been forgiven and His resurrection pointed to my justification\n\nP - God thank you for forgiving and justifying me to your Father!",
