          "ocr_text": "March 15\nS- You shall consecrate them that they may be holy and whatever touches them must be holy. Ex 30:29\nO- In the context of this passage, the people are to consecrate themselves and the articles do not consecrate or make people holy. Only the sacrifice does and even the priests die if they aren't sanctified. Only Jesus could make the unclean clean. He is the fulfillment of the laws\nA- Only Jesus can make me clean. No one else. I must live to worship him.\nP- Jesus, thank you that you were the perfect sacrifice and the high priest that has made a way for me to be with you.\n\nMarch 16\nS- Then the righteous will answer him saying Lord when did we see you hungry and feed you or thirsty and give you drink or naked and clothe you or sick or in prison and visit you and the king will answer he them. Assurely I say to you inasmuch as you did it to the least of these you did it unto me. Matt 25:37-40\nO- Jesus I identify with the poor, imprisoned, sick, hungry and thirsty. The righteous didn't identify the poor with Jesus.\nA- The poor are always with us. How can I help the poor? 10% of budget should go to poor w/ conditions of Timothy.\nP- God help me to be a faithful steward of all you have given to me.",
