          "ocr_text": "March 11\n\nS- Therefore let these who call according to the will of God commit their souls to Him in doing good, as to a faithful creator. I Pet 4:19\n\nO- Peter constantly speaks of suffering and he was the one who told Jesus he couldn't allow Jesus to suffer and get rebuked. He got crucified upside down.\n\nA- I need to commit my soul to Christ. He is able to help all things about to me.\n\nP- God I feel junk. I didn't get to go to Myanmar BTC is low, I have no money. This is so sad.\n\nMarch 12\n\nS- Resist him steadfast in the faith knowing that the same suffering are experienced by your brotherhood in the world. I Pet 5:8\n\nO- All of life is suffering so chose what you are willing to suffer for.\n\nA- I shouldn't live to avoid suffering but I shouldn't pursue it either.\n\nP- God give me wisdom of if I am to go to Myanmar. I know you have something for me there. Direct my life and steps.\n\nMarch 13\n\nG- As his divine power has given to all things that pertain to life and godliness through the knowledge of him who called us by glory and virtue. By which have been given to us exceedingly great and precious promises that through these you may be partakers of the divine nature having escaped the corruption that is late world through lust. II Pet 1:3,9\n\nO- Lust traps and corrupts us. Through knowledge of him we can be godly and partake of the divine nature.\n\nA- I\u0026C I spend time in the Word God will bless and give me favor\n\nP- Lord help me to love you first. Help me to escape!\n\nMarch 14\n\nS- For he who lacks these things is short sighted even to blindness and has forgotten that he was cleansed by his own sins. Therefore brethren be even more diligent to make your call and election sure. As if you do these things you will never stumble II Pet 1:9,10\n\nO- Diligence faith= Victorious knowledge self called, perseverance godliness, a brotherly kindness. If I don't have these things I forgotten I've been cleansed.\n\nA- I need to be grateful Jesus saved and cleansed me.\n\nP- God thank you for your grace in my life.",
