        },
        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T00:52:22.381659+00:00",
          "date_precision": "day",
          "id": "8a387f84-afc7-447f-af97-872c84c88360",
          "import_batch_id": "3ee87fcd-f0ef-4152-94b0-d584085b4ee6",
          "import_seq": null,
          "journal_date": "2025-04-17",
          "ocr_text": "April 17\nS- But I say to you I will not drink of this fruit of the vine from now on until that day when I drink it new with you in my father's kingdom. Matt 26:29\nO- There was a change in the feast of Passover that happened after Jesus died and rose again. The Resurrection marked the entrance of a New kingdom on earth. A deliverance from the bondage of the world. A stripping away of bondage of toil but also from luxuries. To worship in the wilderness.\nA- Jesus has delivered me from sin and its penalties. I can live w/ supernatural provision\nP- Give me appreciation and faith to eat manna and drink from the ROCK.\n\nApril 18\nS- Pete said to Him, \"Even if I have to die with you I will not deny you\" and so said all the disciples. 14 26:35\nO- The apostles love of christ can only be seen through the depravity and cruelty of the cross. To forgive someone who insults you is one thing. But can you forgive \u0026 love someone? What about insults, then slanders you to others. What about it, salt, slander, then weaponize that slander to threaten you? Then harm you? Then humiliate \u0026 harm \u0026 kill you? Could you forgive? Christ not only forgave but He loved. Then the cross is examined against the dark canvas of the cruelty and depravity of man, ever the love of the Father can be understood. But not expected. To experience the power and beauty of the cross the backdrop of the dark canvas of the cross against the backdrop of the dark canvas of. To see the beauty of the cross against the dark canvas\nA- of the Father can be understood. But not expected. To experience the power and beauty of the cross the backdrop of the dark canvas of the cross against the backdrop of the dark canvas of. To see the beauty of the cross against the dark canvas\nP- God help me to see myself in the light \u0026 comparison of your grace\n\nApril 19\nS- And the graves were opened and many bodies of the saints who had fallen asleep were raised, and coming out of the graves after his resurrection they went into the holy city and appeared to many. Matt 27:52\nO- This event is only recorded in matthew and I wonder why it was not recorded in any other gospel.\nA- Jesus has power to raise us into incorruptible bodies and He will one day\nP- God help me to keep my eyes focused on the resurrection and what you have prepared \u0026 those who love you.\n\nApril 20\nS- His countenance was like lightning and his clothes as white as snow. Matt 28:3\nO- Jesus resurrected Rm did not leave behind a dead body.\nA- Even as Christ rose from the dead, so we will rise from the dead.\nP- Lord help us to keep our eyes focused on your return and on the resurrection you have promised to us.\n\nApril 21\nS- And they continued steadfastly in the apostles doctrine fellowship, breaking bread and prayers. Acts 2:42\nO- When people were added attention was given to doctrine hanging out, eating together \u0026 praying.\nA- How can we live like the early church? Seems impossible. People don't study. Don't have time to fellowship \u0026 study. They don't study.\nP- God please help us to do these things steadfastly.",
