          "ocr_text": "April 12\nS- Behold, you desire truth in the inward parts, and in the hidden part you will make me to know wisdom. Ps 51:6\nO- God is about the six on the outside but whats going on on the inside. God will bring me wisdom from the part of me that is hidden\nA- If I give God the hidden part of me, He will give me wisdom in exchange.\nP- God I give you my weaknesses, sin and failures Please restore my mind will and emotions.\n\nApril 13\nS- Offer to God thanksgiving and pay your vows the the Most High Call upon me in the day of trouble. I will deliver you and you shall glorify me. Ps 50:14,15\nO- God wants my thanks \u0026 offerings. He promises that He will deliver me.\nA- God I feel trapped in this down market. I will thank you for all my blessings. Give you the P- I like you deserve. Please rescue and save me. I trust in you.\n\nApril 14\nS- And you will seek me and find me when you search for me with all your heart. Jer 29:13\nO- Finding God is a matter of the heart. God wants all of me and not my leftovers.\nA- I will give God the first of my time in the day first in my week (first my treasure by the title first) before spending and first in my energy.\nP- God help me to put you first before everything\n\nApril 15\nS- For I know the thoughts that I think toward you, says the Lord, thoughts of Peace and not of evil, to give you a future and a hope. Jer:29:11\nO- God thinks of me and His thoughts are good. Of peace and a future and hope. The sabbath is a reflection of the time of rest we will have in eternity w/ the Lord.\nA- I will take more time to be intentional to enjoy time with Jesus and family. To rest relax and reflect on His blessings.\nP- God thank you that you love me. and want me to be worthy line and think of me often.\n\nApril 16\nS- I charge you therefore before God and the Lord Jesus Christ who will judge the living and the dead at his appearing and his kingdom: II Tim 4:1\nO- There is a day coming where Christ will establish his kingdom on earth and be the ruler of all\nA- I will serve the Lord with gladness while it is still a choice to do so.\nP- Thank you for being patient with me even when I don't put you first.",
